[1ae96b8 | 2026-07-04 13:20:52 UTC] Michael Fellinger <michael.fellinger@iohk.io>

  * Fix Tk::Tile::Style.configure silently discarding its options hash

    Style.configure(style = nil, options = {}) is meant to accept a bare options
    hash as the first argument (like Style.map), but its hash-detection branch was
    `(style; style = nil)` -- a bare `style` void expression where it should have
    been `options = style`. So Style.configure(foo: bar) threw the hash away and
    configured nothing. Mirror the corrected Style.map form. Lint/Void flagged the
    dead expression. Suite green (380).

