[95d6a78 | 2026-07-04 12:30:55 UTC] Michael Fellinger <michael.fellinger@iohk.io>

  * Fix broken Tk::Lower / Tk::Raise stacking-order modules

    Both modules paired a same-named instance method with a `module_function`
    def of the same name, so the second def clobbered the first (Lint/DuplicateMethods):
    
    - Lower.lower was `def lower(below = None)` after module_function: wrong arity
      (Lower.lower(self, below) -> ArgumentError given 2, expected 0..1) and
      referenced an undefined local `window`. Completely broken; no coverage.
    - Raise#raise (the public delegator) was overwritten by the module_function
      `raise(window, above)`, so the instance path bound `above` to `window`.
    
    Nothing includes these modules (Widget defines #raise/#lower itself and calls
    the module functions), so the instance delegators were dead. Rewrite each to
    the destroy.rb idiom: a single `def self.NAME(window, ...)` module function.
    This also resolves the `# FIXME: shadow Kernel#raise` note for the module
    (Widget#raise remains the intentional widget API).
    
    Adds spec/ffi-tk/command/{lower,raise}.rb covering both arities and the
    Widget delegators. Also drops the now-fixed Lint/FormatParameterMismatch
    (geometry) and Lint/DuplicateMethods todo entries.

[f74ffdc | 2026-07-04 12:25:07 UTC] Michael Fellinger <michael.fellinger@iohk.io>

  * Fix TkGeometry#to_tcl malformed format strings; populate original

    Two format strings in #to_tcl were broken (no test coverage existed):
    - size-only: '=%dx%d%' raised ArgumentError (incomplete format specifier)
      on every call -> '=%dx%d'
    - position-only: '=+d%+d' silently emitted '=+d<y>' and dropped x (only one
      %-specifier) -> '=%+d%+d'
    
    Also assign the previously-dead Struct member 'original' in #initialize.
    Both output forms verified valid against real Tk wm geometry. Adds
    spec/ffi-tk/geometry.rb (display-independent) covering parse, serialise,
    the two regressions, and full round-trip.

